{
"A drummer must keep a steady beat.": "5889da444d5b",
"A friend says, “Tempo and beat are the same thing.” How would you explain the difference?": "644f341b282a",
"A metronome keeps the beat for you. The mechanical kind has a rod that swings like a pendulum and a weight that slides up the rod to make it slower. A German inventor named Johann Maelzel patented one in 1815, after an earlier design by Dietrich Winkel. Beethoven was soon the first notable composer to write metronome numbers in his music. Even so, the old Italian words such as allegro and andante are only rough guides, and different books give them different numbers.": "311dfcb5a28f",
"A song is played at 120 BPM. How long is one beat, and how many beats are there in 10 seconds?": "cc2578ee7896",
"A waltz has a meter of three beats.": "07162b469896",
"Beats come one after another, each the same length, like the ticks of a clock. We say how fast the beats are with the word tempo, which is Italian for “time.” Tempo is measured in beats per minute, or BPM. At 60 BPM there is exactly one beat every second, like the second hand of a clock. At 120 BPM the beats are twice as fast. For comparison, the resting pulse of a person aged ten or older is 60 to 100 beats per minute, counted in the same unit.": "de8912ab2e63",
"But beats are not all the same. Some feel stronger and some weaker, and the pattern keeps coming back. A set of beats from one strong beat to the next is called a bar, or a measure. The first beat of the bar is the downbeat, and it is usually the strongest. The pattern of strong and weak beats is the meter.": "a70d953e052a",
"Chinese traditional music has its own names for the same idea. The strongest beat is the 板 (bǎn), struck on a wooden clapper. The weaker beats are the 眼 (yǎn), marked with a drumstick. “One 板 and one 眼” means two beats in a bar, and “one 板 and three 眼” means four. In nanguan music, the beats are counted in 撩拍, with its own clapper called the 拍板.": "8da916bf19a6",
"Clap on every beat of the song.": "51ff702bc898",
"Each measure of this song has four beats.": "f1127b7544d6",
"Put an accent on the first beat of the bar.": "9b3013512d1b",
"Put two fingers on your wrist to feel your pulse.": "f467ddcc9c35",
"She practices the piano with a metronome.": "30918711ff44",
"The band played the song at a fast tempo.": "39edf63a62be",
"The most common patterns are twos, threes, and fours. In two beats, the pattern is strong, weak, like a march step. In three beats, it is strong, weak, weak, and you count one-two-three. In four beats, it is strong, weak, medium, weak. Written music shows this with a time signature. In 3/4, the top number says there are three beats in each bar, and the bottom number says that a quarter note gets one beat.": "a8517e1c65ad",
"Think of a song you love and tap your foot along with it. Everyone in the room taps at the same speed, and nobody had to count. What you are tapping is the beat. A beat is the basic unit of time in music, the pulse, and it keeps going whether the melody has a long note or a short one.": "c08d8b93ed89",
